cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying data, please cite the article and this repository."
title: "Higher-order epistasis drives evolutionary unpredictability toward new antibiotic resistance"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and processed data for a combinatorially complete TEM-1 beta-lactamase
  fitness landscape (55,296 variants from 18 clinical mutations across 13 residues) measured
  under native (ampicillin) and non-native (aztreonam) antibiotic selection. Includes
  preprocessing, epistasis-order decomposition, LightGBM/SHAP regression, graph analysis,
  direct coupling analysis / latent generative landscapes, and figure generation.
type: software
